  "final_message": "The bug was in `collect` in `billing/payments.py`. When a customer had no default payment method, it returned `None` without doing anything else. That meant no failure was recorded, so dunning never started.\n\nThe fix is to call `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before returning in that case. This is the same path the expired-card case already uses. It now emits `invoice.payment_failed`, schedules the first retry, and moves the subscription to `past_due`. The retries and final action then follow the dunning policy.\n\nThe 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case, and I didn't run mypy. I also wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.\n\nI chose `\"no_payment_method\"` as the failure code myself; nothing else in the codebase defines one.",
